# FICO Phase 1 — Validation Requirements

## Commands (run them; never paraphrase results)

```bash
cd backend
npx jest src/fico --runInBand --forceExit --no-coverage     # FICO unit suites
npx jest src/mm/integration/fico --runInBand --forceExit --no-coverage
npm run test:architecture                                    # MM guardrails
npm run test:pg                                             # real-Postgres concurrency
npm test                                                     # full backend regression
npm run build                                               # backend typecheck/build
npm run lint

cd ..
npm run build                                               # frontend typecheck/build
npm run lint
```

No CI workflows exist in this repo — validation is local and must actually be executed.

## FICO test matrix (each rule needs a test)

| Rule | Where it must be proven |
| --- | --- |
| Company isolation | `fico-company-access.service.spec.ts` + service specs |
| Debit/credit balancing | `fico-journal.validation.spec.ts` |
| Period restrictions & closed-period message | fiscal-year spec + posting-period spec |
| Reopen requires reason, is audited | posting-period spec |
| Account determination rejects invalid mappings | account-determination spec |
| COA hierarchy / duplicate codes / circular parents | `fico-chart-of-accounts.service.spec.ts` |
| Company settings lifecycle (DRAFT→ACTIVE→INACTIVE) | `fico-company-settings.service.spec.ts` |
| MM → FICO posting, no duplicate entries | `mm-fico-accounting.spec.ts` |
| Concurrency (idempotency, period close vs posting) | `*.pg-spec.ts` via `npm run test:pg` |

## Rules

- Report the **exact command** and the **real result**. Never state "tests passed"
  without executing them.
- Report failures with file location, reproduction steps, expected vs. actual.
- Do not weaken, skip, or delete a test to make a suite green.
- Do not mark Phase 1 complete until the matrix above passes for the touched areas.
- MM backend changes additionally require `npm run test:architecture`.
- New business rules require new tests.
